---
description: Test strategy and conventions for CircleSfera (Vitest, Testing Library, Playwright)
globs: circlesfera-backend/src/**/*.spec.ts, circlesfera-backend/test/**/*.e2e-spec.ts, circlesfera-frontend/src/**/*.test.ts, circlesfera-frontend/src/**/*.test.tsx, e2e/**/*.spec.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

| Layer | Location | Command |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Backend unit | `circlesfera-backend/src/**/*.spec.ts` | `npm test` |
| Backend e2e | `circlesfera-backend/test/*.e2e-spec.ts` — real Postgres + Redis, `fileParallelism: false` | `npm run test:e2e` |
| Frontend unit | `circlesfera-frontend/src/**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}` | `npm test` |
| Composer unit | `create-post/*.test.tsx` — real `es` i18n via `renderWithProviders` | `npx vitest run src/components/create-post/` |
| Composer Playwright | `circlesfera-frontend/e2e/composer-*.spec.ts` — real UI, API stubbed | `npm run test:e2e:composer` |
| Frontend Playwright | `circlesfera-frontend/e2e/*.spec.ts` — SPA journeys, API stubbed | `cd circlesfera-frontend && npm run test:e2e` |
| Browser e2e | root `e2e/*.spec.ts`, Playwright, live Nest | `npm run test:e2e` |

Coverage thresholds are 30% statements/lines. That is a floor, not a target.

Rules:

- A change without a test that **fails before it and passes after** is unverified.
- Test the deny path: forbidden, unauthenticated, wrong owner, missing staff permission, invalid
  payload. Model: `src/auth/guards/admin.guard.spec.ts`.
- Prefer the cheapest level that would actually catch the regression: unit for business rules and
  single-controller HTTP (401, ValidationPipe) via `createControllerApp`; backend e2e for real JWT,
  CSRF, KYC and Postgres; Testing Library for user-visible component behaviour; Playwright for a
  critical journey.
- Keep `e2e/smoke.spec.ts` fast and auth-free — it gates every PR. Root journeys in `e2e/` hit
  live Nest and must not stub `**/api/v1/**`. Do not share `storageState.json` across specs.
- Backend e2e tests share one database and run serially; clean up your fixtures.
- Frontend tests assert what the user sees, not internal state. `src/test/setup.ts`
  mocks `matchMedia` and `IntersectionObserver`. i18n is the real catalogs (`en`
  by default). Composer `create-post` tests pass `{ lng: 'es' }`. Never assert a
  raw `createPost.*` key as visible text.
- Pyramid (what is stubbed vs real): `.ai/core/quality.md`. Composer details: `e2e/COMPOSER_QA.md`.
- Deterministic only: no real clock, no real network, no dependence on file order.
- Never leave `.skip` or `.only`. Never weaken an assertion to make a test pass. Never write a test
  that only exercises its own mocks.
- Never assert a test run you did not perform. If you skipped tests, say why.

Edge cases worth enumerating every time: auth state (anonymous, suspended, banned, scheduled for
deletion), relationships (blocked, muted, private, pending follow, close friends), content state
(`HIDDEN`/`REMOVED`, `MATURE`, premium and locked, expired story), roles, plan state, money failure
paths, and empty/single/last-page lists.

Full strategy: @.ai/agents/qa.md
